    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe title is a little over specific, the problem is certainly deeper. My guess is that it has something to do with cmdwin rewrite. I even observed something similar in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40463#issuecomment-4882697548.\n\nWith the steps below, the wrong variable ends up being renamed.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean -u minimal.lua repro.lua` \n \n- minimal.lua\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({})\n\nvim.o.scrolloff = 4\nvim.o.cmdheight = 0\n\nvim.lsp.config(\"emmylua\", {\n    cmd = { \"emmylua_ls\" },\n    filetypes = { \"lua\" },\n    workspace_required = false,\n})\n\nvim.defer_fn(function()\n    vim.lsp.enable(\"emmylua\")\n\n    vim.cmd(\"norm! 80gg\")\n    vim.cmd(\"norm! zb\")\n    vim.cmd(\"norm! 6l\")\n\n    vim.defer_fn(function()\n        vim.lsp.buf.rename()\n    end, 1000)\nend, 100)\n```\n\n- [repro.lua](https://gist.github.com/igorlfs/7d68c2a6bba7833539c62ee707309494)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe variable from the line that triggered the rename should be renamed.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1938+gaee9105c8a\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.2.11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.28.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This seems to fix the problem:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/buf.lua b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/buf.lua\nindex 41387a14b6..4dce61b999 100644\n--- a/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/buf.lua\n+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/buf.lua\n@@ -800,6 +800,7 @@ function M.rename(new_name, opts)\n \n   -- Compute early to account for cursor movements after going async\n   local cword = vim.fn.expand('<cword>')\n+  local cursor = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(win)\n \n   --- @param range lsp.Range\n   --- @param position_encoding 'utf-8'|'utf-16'|'utf-32'\n@@ -824,6 +825,7 @@ function M.rename(new_name, opts)\n \n     --- @param name string\n     local function rename(name)\n+      vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(win, cursor)\n       local params = util.make_position_params(win, client.offset_encoding) --[[@as lsp.RenameParams]]\n       params.newName = name\n       local handler = client.handlers['textDocument/rename'] or lsp.handlers['textDocument/rename']\n```",
